  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday) \nIssued at 216 AM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThursday and Friday may be very active days as the speed max \napproaching from the eastern Pacific helps to lift the remnant \nconvective circulation from Sonora slowly northeastward over NM.\nPWATs are shown peaking near 1.2\" over the region. As is always the \ncase with monsoon moisture surges, the coverage and intensity of \nconvection will depend on how much instability can develop if \nwidespread cloud cover is present. NBM 48-hour mean QPF shows a \nlarge area between 0.25\" and 0.75\" which is not too impressive. \nNBM 90th percentile values rise above 1.75\" in a few areas so the\npotential is there for locally heavy rainfall and flash flooding.\nQPF values may rise considerably once hi-res model solutions get \na handle on the scenario. Forecast confidence is still moderate \nat this time. \n\nSaturday and Sunday also have potential to be active days as the \nmoisture plume remains squarely over NM with the high east of the \nregion.",
